I disagree with this.  I put a good amount of thought into making sure
that it wouldn't.

All it'd do is protect you against Touch of Death, Death wands and
Death himself.  A Ring Versus Death Magic would, essentially, be a
restricted-focus cloak of magic resistance that goes into a ring slot.
 There are plenty of reasons why you'd rather have magic resistance
than this -- when it comes down to bang-for-the-buck, magic resistance
is one of the most valuable intrinsics you can ask for.

But this particular sort of ring, except in very narrowly-defined
circumstances, is rather useless for most of the game.  Most of the
basic resistance rings are more useful (especially now that winter
wolf cubs are around).  Unless you're unlucky enough to come up
against the textbook Nethack screwing (gnome with a death wand, and
reflection is more useful in that case), you won't need it until you
begin to face off against the big muscle of the game: Master Liches,
the nastier Quest Nemesises, and Rodney.  By that time, most people
have had the chance to get magic resistance.


